    "html": "<p>Two parallel plates are separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span> and connected to a battery of voltage <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span>. A small charged oil droplet with charge <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q\"></span> and mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> remains suspended between the plates. What is the electric field strength required to suspend the droplet?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{V}{qd}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{Vd}{q}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{mg}{q}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{q}{mg}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
